From ec6dc8763f117136150fdb8fb451639fe3b9ffc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USCL agent codex <codex@uscl.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:37:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] USCL: start the wireless link over uscl-bridge, no LAN
 menu

melonDS's LAN link (ENet, UDP 7064) carries DS local wireless between PCs.
For USCL it runs on 127.0.0.1 and uscl-bridge carries it over Steam:

- `--uscl-link host|join` starts it at launch: host binds 127.0.0.1:7064
  (no discovery broadcasts), join connects to 127.0.0.1 and keeps
  retrying until the host is up.
- GDB `monitor uscl-link host|join|off` (qRcmd) switches it while the
  game runs, so a per-game agent can follow the player's Steam session
  (host our own, join a friend's, or free the port before joining).

Shortcut: two players per link (LAN's clients connect to each other by
address, and through the bridge every player is 127.0.0.1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
